.TH STRING.H 3v32 "October 14, 2026" "Vircon32 DevTools 26.04.24" "Vircon32 C Library"
.SH NAME
string.h \- Vircon32 characters, strings and number formatting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqstring.h\(dq
.PP
.BI "bool isdigit( int " c " );"
.BI "bool isxdigit( int " c " );"
.BI "bool isalpha( int " c " );"
.BI "bool isalphanum( int " c " );"
.BI "bool isascii( int " c " );"
.BI "bool islower( int " c " );"
.BI "bool isupper( int " c " );"
.BI "bool isspace( int " c " );"
.BI "int  tolower( int " c " );"
.BI "int  toupper( int " c " );"
.PP
.BI "int  strlen( int* " text " );"
.BI "int  strcmp( int* " text1 ", int* " text2 " );"
.BI "int  strncmp( int* " text1 ", int* " text2 ", int " max_characters " );"
.BI "void strcpy( int* " dest_text ", int* " src_text " );"
.BI "void strncpy( int* " dest_text ", int* " src_text ", int " max_characters " );"
.BI "void strcat( int* " initial_text ", int* " added_text " );"
.BI "void strncat( int* " initial_text ", int* " added_text ", int " max_characters " );"
.PP
.BI "void itoa( int " value ", int* " result_text ", int " base " );"
.BI "void ftoa( float " value ", int* " result_text " );"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
A Vircon32 string is an array of words, one character per word,
terminated by a 0 word; it is passed as an
.BR int* .
Character codes 0 to 255 follow Windows-1252, the encoding of the BIOS
font. None of these functions checks the size of the buffer it writes
to.
.SS Characters
.TP
.BR isdigit ", " isxdigit
Decimal digit; hexadecimal digit (either case).
.TP
.BR isalpha ", " isalphanum
ASCII letter; ASCII letter or digit.
.RB ( isalphanum
is this library's name for C's
.BR isalnum .)
.TP
.B isascii
A code from 0 to 127.
.TP
.BR islower ", " isupper
A lowercase or uppercase letter, including the accented letters of
Windows-1252 (codes 224 to 254 and 192 to 222, except 247 and 215).
.TP
.B isspace
Space, newline, carriage return or tab.
.TP
.BR tolower ", " toupper
Convert the case of a letter, accented ones included; any other code
is returned unchanged.
.SS Strings
.TP
.B strlen
The number of characters before the terminator.
.TP
.BR strcmp ", " strncmp
Compare two strings (at most
.I max_characters
characters for
.BR strncmp ),
returning 0 when equal, or the difference between the first two
characters that differ (negative when
.I text1
sorts first).
.B strncmp
with
.I max_characters
below 1 returns 0.
.TP
.B strcpy
Copy
.I src_text
with its terminator into
.IR dest_text .
Returns nothing (C's returns
.IR dest_text ).
.TP
.B strncpy
Copy at most
.I max_characters
characters, then always write a terminator: up to
.IR max_characters "+1"
words are written. This differs from C, which writes exactly
.I max_characters
words, padding with zeros and leaving the result unterminated when the
source is too long. Does nothing when
.I max_characters
is below 1.
.TP
.B strcat
Append
.I added_text
to
.IR initial_text .
.TP
.B strncat
Append at most
.I max_characters
characters, then a terminator.
.SS Numbers
.TP
.B itoa
Write
.I value
as text in base 2 to 16 (digits above 9 are uppercase letters). Only
in base 10 is the value taken as signed: other bases show the 32-bit
pattern, so
.B itoa( \-1, text, 16 )
writes
.BR FFFFFFFF .
A base outside 2 to 16 writes nothing. At most 33 words are written
(32 binary digits and the terminator).
.TP
.B ftoa
Write
.I value
in decimal with up to 5 decimals, rounded, and without trailing zeros
.RB ( 2.5 ", " \-0.125 ", " 3 ).
A rounding that carries into the whole part is handled
.RB ( 0.999999
writes
.BR 1 ).
There is no exponent notation. The value must be within the range of an
.B int
(see BUGS).
.SH NOTES
There are no
.BR strchr ,
.BR strstr ,
.BR atoi ,
.BR sprintf
or other standard string functions here; v32c++'s C library adds them
for C programs (see
.BR v32libc (3v32)).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vircon32 (3v32),
.BR video.h (3v32),
.BR string.hpp (3v32)
.SH BUGS
.B ftoa
converts the whole part of the value to an
.BR int .
A value of 2147483648 or more, or below \-2147483648, cannot be
converted, and
.B ftoa
does not return: it writes
.BR \-2147483648.
and then keeps appending
.B 0
characters without end, far past the buffer. A
.B float
cannot hold 2147483647 exactly, so
.B 2147483647.0
is 2147483648.0 and hangs too. Compare the value against that range first.
.PP
A negative value that rounds to zero keeps its sign:
.B ftoa( \-0.000001, text )
writes
.BR \-0 .
.PP
Headers before the 2026 fix, including the one in the DevTools 26.04.24
sources, get the carry wrong:
.B ftoa( 0.999999, text )
writes
.BR 0.1 ,
and 1.999999 writes
.BR 1.1 .
This page describes the fixed header
.RB ( string.h ,
file version still 2025/04/08).
.SH AUTHOR
The Vircon32 standard library was written by Javier Carracedo
.RI ( Carra ).
This manual page was written by Matthew Haas for the v32c++ project.
